WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.040
- Alright, I'm really excited about Jexi.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.590
So you play a guy whose life

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.070
is taken over by his phone right?

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:05.903
- [Adam] Yeah.

00:00:05.903 --> 00:00:06.890
- Are you addicted to
your phone in real life?

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.480
- We all are people, don't
try to hide it, okay.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.608
I'm a real addict.

00:00:12.608 --> 00:00:13.441
- [Kelly] Really?

00:00:13.441 --> 00:00:14.274
- Yeah, well, I think everybody,

00:00:14.274 --> 00:00:16.110
I don't know how to drive anywhere.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:16.943
- Oh, my husband--

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:18.830
- Like, if I don't get
directions from my phone

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.900
I don't go there.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.790
- I know and it drives my husband nuts.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.707
He's like "Why do you use your phone?

00:00:23.707 --> 00:00:25.507
"You know, what if something
happens to your phone

00:00:25.507 --> 00:00:26.880
"you're not even gonna know where to go!"

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.251
And I'm like, "I'll find it."

00:00:28.251 --> 00:00:29.084
- Yeah.

00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:30.290
- It'll find, it'll be there.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.100
- You won't find it.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:32.933
You won't find it.

00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:34.560
- [Kelly] I am always on Waze.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.843
- Me too, Waze.

00:00:35.843 --> 00:00:37.820
And then like, I won't be
able to find my way home.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:38.810
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.590
- Like literally, I'm going home

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.190
I'm at a place where I know where I'm at.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.480
And then try to find my way home

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.150
I'm like I just gotta punch it into Waze.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.040
'Cause what if I have
to spend two and half

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.860
more minutes more in the car?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.820
I'd rather take 11 left, very
dangerous left hand turns.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.010
- To get there.
- To get there.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.570
- Just with ease.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.010
- Just like (panicked yelling)

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.700
- Do you feel like you've
switched from childhood?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.280
I feel like I knew phone numbers,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.580
I knew addresses, I knew everything,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.840
how to get anywhere when I was kid.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.360
Like on my bike or walking or whatever.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.810
Now like as an adult I am now a toddler

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.770
who knows none of that.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.650
I don't know anyone's number.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.630
I know my husbands.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.840
- I don't, yeah, I
don't really know anyone

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.287
even my parents they don't
have a home phone anymore.

00:01:20.287 --> 00:01:21.360
- [Kelly] 'Cause why?

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.470
- Yeah, no one does, landlines are dead.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.744
- I know Archaic if you will.

00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:27.854
- Like Bell, the Bell
company, they're pissed.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.790
(laughing loudly)

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.590
- Jeff Bell or whoever that guy was.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:33.403
He's bummed.

00:01:33.403 --> 00:01:34.640
- Oh my god, y'all
don't have a home phone?

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:35.473
This is your mom?

00:01:35.473 --> 00:01:36.814
- This is my mom and dad
right here by the way.

00:01:36.814 --> 00:01:40.430
(crowd applauding)

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.760
- I was bragging on them backstage

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.500
'cause you did so awesome with this one,

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.490
he's so loved.
- Oh, thank you.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.240
- Literally no one has gotten

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.890
that kind of applause yet, that's insane.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.119
- Oh I paid them.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:51.640
(audience laughing)

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.473
- [Kelly] Good mom, see.

00:01:52.473 --> 00:01:53.306
- Yup.

00:01:53.306 --> 00:01:55.260
- So wait, you and your family recently,

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.250
you celebrated Adam DeVine day?

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.967
- Yeah, yeah. I shot my Netflix special

00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:02.867
"Adam DeVine's Best Time Of Our Lives"

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.209
On, one person saw it cool.

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:07.069
(audience laughing)

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:08.520
- You were supposed to applaud there.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.408
But they gave me, the mayor
gave me my own day in Omaha.

00:02:12.408 --> 00:02:15.045
- What, that's cool!
- Yeah, cool.

00:02:15.045 --> 00:02:16.715
- Oh my god.
- Yeah.

00:02:16.715 --> 00:02:17.548
- I didn't get a day.

00:02:17.548 --> 00:02:18.520
- You'll get a key.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:19.611
You'll get something better than a day.

00:02:19.611 --> 00:02:21.160
- [Kelly] I got a key, I want a day.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.980
- I thought it was a day every year.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.005
I thought every November
10th I'm getting it.

00:02:25.005 --> 00:02:26.354
That's what I was telling people.

00:02:26.354 --> 00:02:27.480
I relooked at the plague they gave me.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.700
Just the one day.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.533
- [Kelly] It's just the one day.

00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:30.517
(all laugh)

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.350
- They're like, We're gonna
do something else next year.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.730
- I think you have to
like discover a world,

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.310
or lead the country. (laughs)

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.650
All right I'm sure you all saw

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:38.870
Adam preform at the
Emmy awards last month.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.304
It was incredible.

00:02:40.304 --> 00:02:41.137
- [Adam] Well, thank you.

00:02:41.137 --> 00:02:43.070
- [Kelly] Here's the funny part of it.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.120
You got, you were under attack for,

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.620
first of all the greatest thing ever.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:50.220
- I was under attack guys, I was attacked.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.440
Well, they, Variety
said that I lip synced.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.610
- Which by the way just means
that you're that bad ass.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.560
- Well thank you for that.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.080
But I sang that and I was pretty bummed.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.800
- No I know, that's happened to me before.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.195
I was like, I wanted to
call this lady named Lisa.

00:03:06.195 --> 00:03:09.367
- I feel like any real
singer would have been like,

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:11.937
"oh no he sang that, you could tell."

00:03:11.937 --> 00:03:13.630
- No, but that's what I'm saying,

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.500
it was actually a good thing.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.930
I got so mad about it when
it happened to me years ago,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.920
'cause I was like, "I just
worked my tail off on stage!"

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.900
And somebody said that, and
then everybody was like,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.678
well maybe that just
means you did it so well

00:03:24.678 --> 00:03:25.511
that people thought it had to have been--

00:03:25.511 --> 00:03:26.490
- Well by the way,

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.920
if I'm ever asked to do
anything like that again,

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.640
I'm more than happy to lip sync.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.750
That would take away
like all the pressure.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.000
- Oh my gosh right and running around?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.790
- Yeah it's like, a full day
of rehearsal the day before

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.680
and I'm just like trying
to learn dance moves.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.440
And I'm not a real dancer or singer.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.367
So I'm like not in my wheel--

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.560
- But that's what makes it awesome.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.130
- It's what makes it fun.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.360
- That's the best part.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.330
- Where, I feel like
me out there doing that

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.336
it gives like, anyone hope.

00:03:52.336 --> 00:03:53.750
(audience laugh)

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.590
- That's how I feel.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.892
- It's just a guy out
there whose mute, he's like

00:03:56.892 --> 00:03:58.123
(murmurs) maybe I could do that?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.387
- [Kelly] He can't even
talk but he's like,

00:04:00.387 --> 00:04:02.780
"I can get this!"
- "I wanna be a singer!"

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.520
- [Kelly] Alright well my favorite part,

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.370
was the giant Meryl Streep head.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.770
It was a little psychotic
and she had no soul

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.050
'cause the eyes were gone.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:13.010
But it was, the eyes were dark.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:13.843
They were dark, but that
was my favorite part.

00:04:13.843 --> 00:04:15.444
- [Adam] Weirdly, that was
Meryl Streep doing that.

00:04:15.444 --> 00:04:16.490
(audience laughing)

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.990
- She does everything, she's
also an amazing juggler.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.210
- She also can turn her eyes black.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.470
- Yeah.
- She's talented.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.803
- She's really talented.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.260
- This is also something
I found out about you

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.460
that I did not know,

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:31.520
so you were in like a horrific
accident when you were a kid,

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.013
and it was, a truck hit you.

00:04:33.013 --> 00:04:33.846
- Cement truck.

00:04:33.846 --> 00:04:36.320
- A big cement truck.
- A bigger kind of truck.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.307
- Dang!
- Not a Ford, not a little --

00:04:37.307 --> 00:04:38.477
- [Kelly] Not even like an F150.

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:41.350
- Not an F150, not an F250.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:42.430
- [Kelly] Oh my god, how did it --

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.800
- Bigger.
- How did it even,

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.830
How did that shape you?

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.402
Because you've gotta be,
you had to have so much--

00:04:46.402 --> 00:04:47.311
- Mangled me.

00:04:47.311 --> 00:04:48.144
(audience laugh)

00:04:48.144 --> 00:04:50.433
- I was a very weird
shape after that, obtuse.

00:04:54.589 --> 00:04:56.000
- All the geometric angles.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.789
- A lot of weird angles.

00:04:57.789 --> 00:05:01.617
- No I meant like (laughs) not physically!

00:05:01.617 --> 00:05:03.720
I meant like mentally and emotionally.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.210
That had to kind of change things.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:07.043
You're funny.

00:05:07.043 --> 00:05:08.093
- For sure.

00:05:08.093 --> 00:05:08.926
(all laugh)

00:05:08.926 --> 00:05:12.243
Well, no, absolutely, I think like yeah,

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.010
I like what I'm now

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.370
I'm like happy that it happened

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.160
because I don't think I'd
be doing what I'm doing

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.760
and it also, it like
gave me the confidence,

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.920
'cause I had to re learn how to walk,

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.200
I couldn't walk it was a two year process

00:05:30.337 --> 00:05:31.900
to gain the strength back in my legs

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.120
and learn how to walk again.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.800
And I lost all the muscle and I shattered

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.660
everything from my knees down.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.430
So I had to like, fully relearn.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.647
That's like really hard to do, turns out.

00:05:41.647 --> 00:05:43.080
- Turns out!

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.820
- You think on paper, yeah!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.723
One step, another step, you got it!

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.100
You figured it out when you were one

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.860
you can figure it out now.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.120
It was very hard and so now I'm like,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.160
I can do anything when I can't.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.710
But I have that confidence.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:05:59.800
- But you can, that's what I love about,

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:00.990
I think that a lot of

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.920
like creative people have odd things

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:03.810
that happen to them in childhood

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.727
that are horrible or whatever
'cause it kind of shapes you

00:06:05.727 --> 00:06:07.210
and it makes you this creative person.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.931
You can, make fun of
yourself, self deprecation.

00:06:09.931 --> 00:06:10.764
- For sure.

00:06:10.764 --> 00:06:12.080
- [Kelly] And even have like, no shame.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.720
You're just like "I'm in it, why not?"

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.670
- And also like, I feel
like, my parents being here,

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:17.990
what's up mom and dad.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.017
Angle on them.

00:06:19.017 --> 00:06:22.740
And they also then were like,

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.260
'cause it's a blue collar
family from the Midwest

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.440
we didn't know anybody in Hollywood,

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.290
we didn't know that you
could even like truly make

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.620
a career out of this.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.840
If that's what you call this.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.477
It's a career mom!

00:06:35.477 --> 00:06:36.526
- It's a real job!

00:06:36.526 --> 00:06:39.087
- Then they got on
board and they were like

00:06:39.087 --> 00:06:41.767
"Whatever you wanna do, you didn't die!

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:43.327
"Whatever you wanna do!"

00:06:43.327 --> 00:06:44.160
- See this all worked out in the end!

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.110
- "You can be a doctor!"

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.040
And I'm like "what about
a stand up comedian?"

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.290
And they're like, "okay."

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:50.497
- [Kelly] Sure, that one too.

00:06:50.497 --> 00:06:53.110
- "If that's what you wanna be." (laughs)

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:56.100
- So, what do you think, 'cause I always,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.520
people always ask me this question and

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.160
I always kinda start questioning myself

00:06:59.160 --> 00:06:59.993
later on that day,

00:06:59.993 --> 00:07:02.640
but what do you think, if
that wouldn't have happened,

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.380
do you think that this
would have been your path?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.110
Or do you think you would
have done something else?

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.915
- For sure, I would be
like a cool wedding DJ.

00:07:09.915 --> 00:07:12.530
(all laugh loudly)

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.140
And I would do a lot of bad beat boxing,

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.693
you know like, Jacob and
Linda, getting hitched!

00:07:17.693 --> 00:07:20.890
(imitates beat box)

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:22.335
Radio edit!

00:07:22.335 --> 00:07:23.873
- I would have been the wedding singer!

00:07:23.873 --> 00:07:25.330
I would have been cool with it!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.040
Wedding receptions are the best.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.570
- I wanna go right to like,

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:30.860
the good part of the
wedding is like the vows,

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:33.700
and then people cry and then
immediately start drinking.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.940
That's what I want my wedding to be.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.490
- I eloped, and was like "bye!"

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:43.020
- I'm gonna give everyone
camel backs filled with wine,

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.512
or whatever type of booze.

00:07:44.512 --> 00:07:46.190
(cheers)

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.770
So they could just suck their
way through the wedding!

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.320
- I would come to your wedding!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.770
- You're invited!

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:56.230
- You have to sing though,

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:57.230
you do have to sing.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.230
- You weren't a wedding singer though,

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.920
but you did have an interesting job that

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:02.753
we actually have in common.

00:08:02.753 --> 00:08:03.760
You were a tele-marketer.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:04.593
- Oh you were a tele-marketer too?

00:08:04.593 --> 00:08:05.950
- I was.
- Oh dang!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.750
- I was a tele-marketer
for the comedy club

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:08.831
I cocktail waitress for

00:08:08.831 --> 00:08:09.664
on the weekends.
- Oh you did that.

00:08:09.664 --> 00:08:11.340
- So I got to kind of
sell them free tickets,

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.850
but there's a two drink minimum.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.510
- I did a lot of weird,
I sold Time Life books

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.440
over the phone, I sold steaks.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.420
- Steaks, Omaha Steaks.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.880
- Omaha Steaks is where I worked.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:21.931
- Yeah.

00:08:21.931 --> 00:08:23.560
- It would be a lot of me--

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.090
- Is that like, how you
sell that, mine was easier.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.430
- I would call and my main
thing, it's so stupid,

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:29.660
I would take a piece of paper,

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.170
and this was like my closer,

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:32.490
I would wiggle the piece of paper

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.760
in front of my face which
is where the headset was

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.897
and then I go, "sorry,
excuse me, my managers here.

00:08:38.897 --> 00:08:43.330
"What's that, no I
can't, really, no, what?"

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.717
And then I get back and I'm like,

00:08:44.717 --> 00:08:47.047
"I'm so sorry, I can't
believe this is happening,

00:08:47.047 --> 00:08:50.180
"But this just came in from upstairs,"

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.997
One floor building.

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:53.997
"This came in from upstairs,

00:08:53.997 --> 00:08:56.651
"We're gonna cut the price
of those filets by half."

00:08:56.651 --> 00:08:59.927
(audience laughing)

